config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_SYNC_TIMER
	bool "Domoticz plugin: sync timer"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_REQUESTS
	default n
	help
		periodic synchronisation of timers and switches between Domoticz and external devices (it uses requests for the endpoints it synchronises).

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/Update_timer, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		Setup -> Hardware -> sync timer, enter the broker and the devices to synchronise.

		Upstream ships no license file: the README is installed with the plugin. The
		repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a pinned commit of
		the default branch.
